## Functional form of `median`: median after sorting.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `l`: the list to reduce. Read only.
##
## ## Retorno
## The median as `T` (an even length averages the two central values with
## truncation), or `donum T` when `l` is empty. Borrows `l`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var xs as list of int is [3, 1, 4]
## calling median with xs    # 3
## ```
weave median shard T where T: Num and T: Ordered with l as list of T into T:
    let n as int is calling l.len
    if n == 0:
        return donum T
    var s as list of T is list of T
    defer banish s
    for x in l:
        calling s.push with x
    var i as int is 0
    while i < n:
        var j as int is i + 1
        while j < n:
            var left as T is s at j
            var right as T is s at i
            let c as int is calling left.cmp with right
            if c < 0:
                let tmp as T is s at i
                set s at i is (s at j)
                set s at j is tmp
            set j is j + 1
        set i is i + 1
    let mid as int is n / 2
    if (n % 2) == 1:
        return s at mid
    return ((s at (mid - 1)) + (s at mid)) / 2

## Functional form of `mode`: most frequent value.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `l`: the list to reduce. Read only.
