## ## Parámetros
## - `l`: the list to scan. Read only.
##
## ## Retorno
## `true` when `l` never decreases. Borrows `l`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var xs as list of int is [1, 2, 3]
## calling is_sorted_asc with xs    # true
## ```
weave is_sorted_asc shard T where T: Ordered with l as list of T into bool:
    let n as int is calling l.len
    if n <= 1:
        return true
    var i as int is 0
    while i < (n - 1):
        var a as T is l at i
        var b as T is l at (i + 1)
        let c as int is calling a.cmp with b
        if c > 0:
            return false
        set i is i + 1
    return true

## Functional form of `is_sorted_desc`: non-ascending order test.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `l`: the list to scan. Read only.
##
## ## Retorno
## `true` when `l` never increases. Borrows `l`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var xs as list of int is [3, 2, 1]
## calling is_sorted_desc with xs    # true
## ```
weave is_sorted_desc shard T where T: Ordered with l as list of T into bool:
    let n as int is calling l.len
    if n <= 1:
        return true
    var i as int is 0
    while i < (n - 1):
        var a as T is l at i
        var b as T is l at (i + 1)
        let c as int is calling a.cmp with b
        if c < 0:
            return false
        set i is i + 1
    return true

## Functional form of `all_positive`: strict positivity test.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `l`: the list to scan. Read only.
##
## ## Retorno
## `true` when every element is `> 0`; the empty list gives `true`. Borrows `l`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var xs as list of int is [3, 1, 2]
## calling all_positive with xs    # true
## ```
weave all_positive shard T where T: Num and T: Ordo with l as list of T into bool:
    let zero as T is donum T
    for x in l:
        if x <= zero:
            return false
    return true

## Functional form of `all_zero`: zero-sentinel test.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `l`: the list to scan. Read only.
##
## ## Retorno
## `true` when every element equals `donum T`; the empty list gives `true`.
## Borrows `l`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var xs as list of int is [0, 0]
## calling all_zero with xs    # true
## ```
weave all_zero shard T where T: Donum and T: Par with l as list of T into bool:
    let zero as T is donum T
    for x in l:
        if x != zero:
            return false
    return true

## Functional form of `any_negative`: finds at least one negative element.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `l`: the list to scan. Read only.
##
## ## Retorno
## `true` when some element is `< 0`; the empty list gives `false`. Borrows `l`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var xs as list of int is [3, -1]
## calling any_negative with xs    # true
## ```
weave any_negative shard T where T: Num and T: Ordo with l as list of T into bool:
    let zero as T is donum T
    for x in l:
        if x < zero:
            return true
    return false

## Functional form of `all_in_range`: inclusive range test.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `l`: the list to scan. Read only.
## - `lo`: inclusive lower bound.
## - `hi`: inclusive upper bound.
##
## ## Retorno
## `true` when every element falls in `[lo, hi]`. Borrows `l`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var xs as list of int is [1, 3, 5]
## calling all_in_range with xs, 1, 5    # true
## ```
weave all_in_range shard T where T: Ordered with l as list of T, lo as T, hi as T into bool:
    for x in l:
        let c_lo as int is calling x.cmp with lo
        if c_lo < 0:
            return false
        let c_hi as int is calling x.cmp with hi
        if c_hi > 0:
            return false
    return true

## Functional form of `filter_even`: copy with the even elements.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `l`: the list to filter. Read only.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned `list of T` with the elements where `x % 2 == 0`; release it with
## `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var xs as list of int is [3, 1, 4, 1, 5]
## calling filter_even with xs    # [4]
## ```
weave filter_even shard T where T: Integrum and T: Par with l as list of T into list of T:
    return for x in l when (x % 2) == 0 then x

## Functional form of `filter_odd`: copy with the odd elements.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `l`: the list to filter. Read only.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned `list of T` with the elements where `x % 2 != 0`; release it with
## `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var xs as list of int is [3, 1, 4, 1, 5]
## calling filter_odd with xs    # [3, 1, 1, 5]
## ```
weave filter_odd shard T where T: Integrum and T: Par with l as list of T into list of T:
    return for x in l when (x % 2) != 0 then x

## Functional form of `filter_positive`: copy with the strictly positive
## elements.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `l`: the list to filter. Read only.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned `list of T`; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var xs as list of int is [3, -1, 0]
## calling filter_positive with xs    # [3]
## ```
weave filter_positive shard T where T: Num and T: Ordo with l as list of T into list of T:
    let zero as T is donum T
    return for x in l when x > zero then x

## Functional form of `filter_negative`: copy with the strictly negative
## elements.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `l`: the list to filter. Read only.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned `list of T`; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var xs as list of int is [3, -1, 0]
## calling filter_negative with xs    # [-1]
## ```
weave filter_negative shard T where T: Num and T: Ordo with l as list of T into list of T:
    let zero as T is donum T
    return for x in l when x < zero then x

## Functional form of `filter_in_range`: copy with the elements inside
## `[lo, hi]`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `l`: the list to filter. Read only.
## - `lo`: inclusive lower bound.
## - `hi`: inclusive upper bound.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned `list of T`; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var xs as list of int is [3, 1, 4, 1, 5]
## calling filter_in_range with xs, 2, 4    # [3, 4]
## ```
weave filter_in_range shard T where T: Ordered with l as list of T, lo as T, hi as T into list of T:
    var flags as list of bool is list of bool
    defer banish flags
    for x in l:
        let c_lo as int is calling x.cmp with lo
        let c_hi as int is calling x.cmp with hi
        calling flags.push with (c_lo >= 0 and c_hi <= 0)
    var keep as list of int is list of int
    defer banish keep
    var i as int is 0
    for f in flags:
        if f:
            calling keep.push with i
        set i is i + 1
    return for k in keep then (l at k)

## @deprecated Use `filter_in_range` instead.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `l`: the list to filter. Read only.
## - `lo`: inclusive lower bound.
## - `hi`: inclusive upper bound.
##
## ## Retorno
## Same as `filter_in_range`; kept only for compatibility.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var xs as list of int is [3, 1, 4, 1, 5]
## calling filter_range with xs, 2, 4    # [3, 4]
## ```
weave filter_range shard T where T: Ordered with l as list of T, lo as T, hi as T into list of T:
    var flags as list of bool is list of bool
    defer banish flags
    for x in l:
        let c_lo as int is calling x.cmp with lo
        let c_hi as int is calling x.cmp with hi
        calling flags.push with (c_lo >= 0 and c_hi <= 0)
    var keep as list of int is list of int
    defer banish keep
    var i as int is 0
    for f in flags:
        if f:
            calling keep.push with i
        set i is i + 1
    return for k in keep then (l at k)

## Functional form of `map_double`: copy with every element doubled.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `l`: the list to map. Read only.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned `list of T`; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var xs as list of int is [3, 1, 2]
## calling map_double with xs    # [6, 2, 4]
## ```
weave map_double shard T where T: Num with l as list of T into list of T:
    return for x in l then (x * 2)

## Functional form of `map_square`: copy with every element squared.
##
## ## Parámetros
